\title{Feast of St. Bartholomew 2025}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2025-08-23}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
  MIHI autem nimis honoráti sunt amíci tui, Deus: nimis confortátus est principátus eórum.
  \br
  EGO autem sicut olíva fructificávi in domo Dómini, sperávi in misericórdia Dei mei: et exspectábo nomen tuum, quóniam bonum est ante conspéctum sanctórum tuórum.
  \br
  Inclína Dómine, aurem tuam ad me, et exáudi me: salvum fac servum tuum, Deus meus, sperántem in te: miserére mihi, Domine, quóniam ad te clamávi tota die.
}
\p{Today our choir at [All Saints Ainslie](https://allsaintsainslie.org.au) sang for Evensong, so I sang my arrangement of Hildegard of Bingen's \em{O Virtus Sapientiae} with a psalm appended during the morning mass. The livestream can be found [here](https://youtu.be/HT71KWbjrlU?t=3199):}
\quote{
  \table{
    \tr{
    \td{O Virtus Sapiéntiæ}
    \td{O Strength of Wisdom!}
    }\tr{
    \td{Quæ circúiens circuísti,}
    \td{Thou who, circling, hast encircled  }
    }\tr{
    \td{Comprehéndendo ómnia in una via quæ habet vitam.}
    \td{Comprehending all things in the one way that hath life.}
  }\tr{
    \td{Tres alas habens:}
    \td{Three wings thou hast: }
  }
  \tr{
      \td{Quarum una in altum volat,}
      \td{The one which soareth on high,}
    }
    \tr{\td{Et áltera de terra sudat,}
    \td{The other sweateth from the Earth}}
    \tr{
        \td{Et tértia úndique volat,}
        \td{And the third flieth everywhere about.}
      }
      \tr{
          \td{Laus tibi sit, sicut te decet, O Sapiéntia.}
          \td{Praise be to thee, as is meet, O Wisdom.}
        }
  }
}
\p{In between the morning mass and evensong, I began rehearsing for our next [Coro](loc-003G) concert. This meant I was singing at the church from morning to night!}
\p{For evensong, I selected the music but our normal director conducted. We sang Morley's fauxbourdon [Magnificat](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CGjV7UCTSzE) and [Nunc Dimittis](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZMBVn7mJiRw), and Tallis' [O Lord give thy Holy Spirit](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zkdg9pFMLYA) as the anthem.}
\quote{
  \poem{
    \line{O Lord, give thy Holy Spirit into our hearts,}
    \line{And lighten our understanding,}
    \line{That we may dwell in the fear of thy Name,}
    \line{All the days of our life;}
    \line{That we may know thee, the only True God:}
    \line{And Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent.}
  }
}